### tag_raw

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"// The children view is built once and is a plain child (a closure would move it out of an FnMut, and isn't Send):\n// children that read signals wrap those parts in reactive_view / reactive_fragment.\ninl tag_raw tag props children : string =\n    inl children = children () |> fragment_to_view\n    tag_text tag props $'\"{ !children }\"'","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  // The children view is built once and is a plain child (a closure would move it out of an FnMut, and isn't Send):
  // children that read signals wrap those parts in reactive_view / reactive_fragment.
  inl tag_raw tag props children : string =
      inl children = children () |> fragment_to_view
      tag_text tag props $'"{ !children }"'
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

### reactive_view

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"// Tag children are built once (see tag_raw), so a signal read at a children's top level doesn't update the view.\n// reactive_view makes `fn` a reactive child: leptos re-runs it when a signal it read changes. Its captures must be\n// Clone (signals, memos, closures, strings), not views.\ninl reactive_view (fn : () -> view) : view =\n    inl fn = fn |> send_wrapper_new\n    $'leptos::prelude::IntoAny::into_any(move || (*!fn)())'","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  // Tag children are built once (see tag_raw), so a signal read at a children's top level doesn't update the view.
  // reactive_view makes `fn` a reactive child: leptos re-runs it when a signal it read changes. Its captures must be
  // Clone (signals, memos, closures, strings), not views.
  inl reactive_view (fn : () -> view) : view =
      inl fn = fn |> send_wrapper_new
      $'leptos::prelude::IntoAny::into_any(move || (*!fn)())'
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

